From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 23:14:23 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Pass an uncompressed packet on as a slice of its frame

Nearly every packet a client sends is under the compression threshold, and each was copied into a
buffer of its own only to drop the leading 0. The decompressor now hands on a retained slice of the
splitter's frame. VPS SG bench: PacketDecompressor.decode 0.85% -> 0.20% of the process.

Holding the event loop wake-ups during the tracker's flush hold was tried in the same run and
dropped: eventfd writes stayed at 1.2% (enableAutomaticFlush still wakes the loop once per
connection) and the bunched tracker packets got a bot kicked by the packet limiter.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/PacketDecompressor.java b/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/PacketDecompressor.java
index c13e0cda44092b64f1d9d9159718c8a4b2de5ecb..80a3d5a9dd34b990c3f4bc5e7cc8cba3cb65f9da 100644
--- a/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/PacketDecompressor.java
+++ b/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/PacketDecompressor.java
@@ -30,7 +30,11 @@ public class PacketDecompressor extends ByteToMessageDecoder {
             int i = packetdataserializer.readVarIntFromBuffer();
 
             if (i == 0) {
-                list.add(packetdataserializer.readBytes(packetdataserializer.readableBytes()));
+                // Athena - a slice of the frame, not a copy: nearly every packet a client sends is under
+                // the threshold, and each was copied into a buffer of its own just to drop the
+                // leading 0. The splitter's frame is itself a retained slice; this holds it until the
+                // packet decoder has read it, as the copy was held.
+                list.add(packetdataserializer.readRetainedSlice(packetdataserializer.readableBytes()));
             } else {
                 if (i < this.treshold) {
                     throw new DecoderException("Badly compressed packet - size of " + i + " is below server threshold of " + this.treshold);
